program	typealias_ref_launder.saw
triple	arm64-apple-darwin
twin	same
expect	error
build	refused	field `r` of `Holder` may not be a reference: `R` names a reference (`&Int`), and references in Saw are PARAMETERS ONLY — a reference borrows storage for the duration of one call and may not escape it (designs 88/106). A `type` alias is not a way past that rule: the walk resolves it
meets_expect	yes
log	"error: field `r` of `Holder` may not be a reference: `R` names a reference (`&Int`), and references in Saw are PARAMETERS ONLY — a reference borrows storage for the duration of one call and may not escape it (designs 88/106). A `type` alias is not a way past that rule: the walk resolves it"
log	"  --> examples/typealias_ref_launder.saw:14:5"
log	"     |"
log	" 14 |     r: R"
log	"     |     ^"
log	"   hint: use the value type (`Int`), or — to hand out storage a type already owns — declare a `borrows` accessor (`... borrows -> &var Int` with `lend`, design 141)"
log	""
log	"error: a value of type `R` may not be a reference: `R` names a reference (`&Int`), and references in Saw are PARAMETERS ONLY — a reference borrows storage for the duration of one call and may not escape it (designs 88/106). A `type` alias is not a way past that rule: the walk resolves it"
log	"  --> examples/typealias_ref_launder.saw:19:23"
log	"     |"
log	" 19 |     let h = Holder(r: R(&x))"
log	"     |                       ^"
log	"   hint: use the value type (`Int`), or — to hand out storage a type already owns — declare a `borrows` accessor (`... borrows -> &var Int` with `lend`, design 141)"
